vivid-nord.yml is a contrast-adjusted version of Vivid's Nord theme:
https://github.com/sharkdp/vivid/blob/master/themes/nord.yml
The original attribution and documented variations are retained in the file.
Vivid is available under MIT or Apache-2.0; this copy uses its MIT license.
See LICENSE-vivid. ls-colors-nord is the pregenerated output of this local
vivid-nord.yml; no Vivid execution is required during configuration rendering.

The Bat, Btop, Glamour, DMS, Kubecolor and Starship profiles use the Nord
palette with local contrast adjustments. The Helix profile inherits Helix's
bundled nord theme instead of vendoring it. The Yazi flavor is vendored from
stepbrobd/nord.yazi with its MIT license and exact provenance in yazi-nord.yazi/ORIGIN.

starship.toml adapts Starship's Pastel Powerline preset with the Nord palette
and a different selection of prompt modules:
https://starship.rs/presets/pastel-powerline.html
The original preset is inspired by the M365Princess Oh My Posh theme.
Copyright (c) 2019-2022, Starship Contributors. See LICENSE-starship.

DMS and Kubecolor assets are portable data only. Their private consumers decide
whether to deploy them; the public theme profile does not enable a desktop.
